Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:18:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ui): keep the Bedrock death screen above server forms

A server form that arrives while the local player is dead replaced the
death screen. Its respawn timer then stopped, and closing the form built a
new death screen without the reason.

The Bedrock 1.26.60.5 gameplay route selector (0x146f42b00, executable
SHA-256 988f6a61403b4381aa41e6c66d64cce441b14e561a9b10f647c2758ef3f2672a)
returns /gameplay/death while the player-alive flag is clear, before it
checks bedtime, data-driven forms, block actors or trading. The respawn
listener (0x146f41e40) sets the flag and recomputes the route, so a form
that arrived meanwhile shows once the player is alive.

Hold both native forms and the Java dialogs that present ordinary forms
until the local player is alive and Java's terrain screen has closed. A
newer form replaces the held one, a close-form request drops it, and a
replaced connection discards it with its listener.

Containers keep their Java behavior because their open state is shared
with the server.

diff --git a/src/main/java/com/viaversion/viafabricplus/bedrock/injection/mixin/features/screen/MixinBedrockDeathScreenForms.java b/src/main/java/com/viaversion/viafabricplus/bedrock/injection/mixin/features/screen/MixinBedrockDeathScreenForms.java
